   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello group,</div><div><br></div><div>I am having an issue extracting real parameters from a model object. The model has 3 sessions and 3 occasions per session (total of 9 occasions). Effort varies per occasion. The model call is as follows:</div><div><br></div><div>fit.t&lt;- secr.fit(captdata, model = list(D ~ Session, g0~t, sigma~g), groups=&quot;Sex&quot;, mask = mask, trace = F,  verify = F, detectfn = 2)</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to look at the occasion-specific real parameters, but I am having some issues doing so. I have tried using a simple call to predict:</div><div><pre><span><span>predict(fit.t, newdata=data.frame(t=1:3), realnames= &quot;g0&quot;)</span></span></pre></div><div>and<br></div><div><pre><span><span>predict(fit.t, newdata=data.frame(Session=1:3,t=1:3))<br><br>But I encounter the following error:<br></span></span><span><span>Error in mat %*% beta[indx] : non-conformable arguments<br><br>I&#39;m sure this is a simple error on my part, but I have not figured it out.<br><br>Any help is much appreciated.<br><br>Colby<br></span></span><span><span></span></span></pre></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "jgN4NAftGwAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2019-01-27T02:24:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: Predicting occasion-specific real parameters",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>&#39;t&#39; is a factor, so needs to be presented as such in newdata. Also you seem to have omitted &#39;g&#39;.</div><div>It&#39;s easier to just use predict(fit.t, all.levels = TRUE) (documentation hidden in ?secr.make.newdata).<br></div><div>This worked for me:<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mask </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mask</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">traps</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ovenCH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> buffer </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">300</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nx </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ovenCH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Sex&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    mask </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mask</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  verify </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>## There were mostly 10 occasions per session in the ovenbird mistnetting<br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> newdata </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> expand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">grid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Session</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levels</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;F&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;M&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> just<br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">levels</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div><br><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Sunday, January 27, 2019 at 1:50:59 PM UTC+13, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">coba...@ucsc.edu</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello group,</div><div><br></div><div>I am having an issue extracting real parameters from a model object. The model has 3 sessions and 3 occasions per session (total of 9 occasions). Effort varies per occasion. The model call is as follows:</div><div><br></div><div>fit.t&lt;- secr.fit(captdata, model = list(D ~ Session, g0~t, sigma~g), groups=&quot;Sex&quot;, mask = mask, trace = F,  verify = F, detectfn = 2)</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to look at the occasion-specific real parameters, but I am having some issues doing so. I have tried using a simple call to predict:</div><div><pre><span><span>predict(fit.t, newdata=data.frame(t=1:3), realnames= &quot;g0&quot;)</span></span></pre></div><div>and<br></div><div><pre><span><span>predict(fit.t, newdata=data.frame(Session=1:3,t=1:3))<br><br>But I encounter the following error:<br></span></span><span><span>Error in mat %*% beta[indx] : non-conformable arguments<br><br>I&#39;m sure this is a simple error on my part, but I have not figured it out.<br><br>Any help is much appreciated.<br><br>Colby<br></span></span><span><span></span></span></pre></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
